1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,229
Can we measure one electrode's potential on its own?

2
00:00:03,229 --> 00:00:03,919
No.

3
00:00:03,919 --> 00:00:11,145
A voltmeter needs two contacts, and the second wire dipping in the solution would itself be a second electrode.

4
00:00:11,145 --> 00:00:14,882
Every measurement is a difference between two electrodes.

5
00:00:14,882 --> 00:00:20,273
So all E nought values are relative, measured against one agreed reference.

